      "ok": true,
      "duplicates": 0,
      "lastReply": "A VPN is a private tunnel between your device and the internet. Everything you send goes through it, scrambled, so nobody in between can read it.\n\nWithout a VPN, your internet provider (or the café Wi-Fi) can see which sites you visit, and those sites see your real address. With a VPN, your data is locked before it leaves your phone or laptop and travels to the VPN's computer. That computer unlocks it and talks to the website for you. The site sees the VPN's address, not yours.\n\nIt's handy on public Wi-Fi and for keeping your browsing private from your provider. It doesn't make you invisible, though: the VPN company can see your activity, so pick one you trust.\n\n9:16 PM",
